      "body": "70 million dollars is the amount the Blue & You Foundation for a Healthier Arkansas has invested in health initiatives across all 75 counties since its founding. These funds support programs that address behavioral health and community wellness throughout the state.\n\nOn October 15, 2026, the foundation surprised five nonprofit organizations with special $25,000 gifts. These gifts were part of the Innovation in Action awards, which mark the 25th anniversary of the foundation. Arkansas Blue Cross and Blue Shield established the Blue & You Foundation in October 2001.\n\nIn 2023, the foundation and Arkansas Blue Cross and Blue Shield committed to improving mental and behavioral health in Arkansas communities. In October of that year, the foundation announced grants totaling 5.9 million dollars to address mental health challenges and substance use among children and young adults. \"We learned about the struggles parents were having, whether it was trying to access services or understanding what was normal teen-age behavior and what was a mental health issue,\" said Dr. Nikki Edge.\n\nOn July 12, the Wolfe Street Foundation hosted a ribbon cutting for its new Youth Empowerment Project and center in Little Rock. The Blue & You Foundation partly funded the center and connected the organization with the UAMS Six Bridges Clinic. Wolfe Street Foundation Executive Director Justin Buck said, \"The Wolfe Street Foundation is proud to partner with the Blue & You Foundation for a Healthier Arkansas to help young Arkansans envision a bright future without the use of drugs or alcohol.\"\n\nOther funded programs address housing and family management. The University District Development Corporation will construct six new affordable single-family homes and 10 duplexes in Little Rock. Restore Hope's 100 Families Initiative will expand into Mississippi, Independence and Jefferson counties to offer collaborative case management. Nonprofit and municipal organizations, as we